WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.431
Every insurer has its own claim form and may ask for something more.

2
00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.578
But some documents are asked for almost every time,

3
00:00:07.764 --> 00:00:10.167
and it is worth gathering them early.

4
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.578
For every claim:

5
00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:16.769
the policy number, the insurer’s claim form filled in and signed,

6
00:00:16.956 --> 00:00:19.904
a copy of the claimant’s ID card or passport,

7
00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:22.563
and the account details for the payment.

8
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:25.125
For a hospital stay:

9
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:29.014
the discharge report, a medical report with the diagnosis,

10
00:00:29.387 --> 00:00:34.157
itemised invoices and receipts, prescriptions and test results for the case,

11
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.931
and the GESY referral if there is one.

12
00:00:39.031 --> 00:00:42.803
For an accident, a short description, a medical report,

13
00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:45.346
the police report if the police were involved,

14
00:00:45.475 --> 00:00:48.945
and a certificate of incapacity if you claim an allowance.

15
00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.616
For a death, the death certificate,

16
00:00:51.744 --> 00:00:56.504
a medical certificate of the cause and the beneficiaries’ IDs.

17
00:00:57.604 --> 00:01:01.923
Tell the insurer as early as you can, because many policies have deadlines,

18
00:01:01.923 --> 00:01:04.151
and keep copies of everything you hand in.

19
00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:08.226
If you are his client, call Giannis before you send the documents,

20
00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:10.618
so you can go through them together.

21
00:01:11.718 --> 00:01:14.945
The checklist is free on farazisgiannis.com,

22
00:01:15.131 --> 00:01:18.927
one page to print or keep on your phone, with no sign-up.
